From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:24:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] ffmpeg: rpi: leave the decode queue when no dst buffer is
 free

A failed destination buffer allocation in the V4L2 request HEVC decoder left the frame queued, and closing the decoder then hung.

Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
---
 ...eave-the-decode-queue-on-dst-failure.patch | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 packages/multimedia/ffmpeg/patches/rpi/0002-v4l2_req-hevc-leave-the-decode-queue-on-dst-failure.patch

diff --git a/packages/multimedia/ffmpeg/patches/rpi/0002-v4l2_req-hevc-leave-the-decode-queue-on-dst-failure.patch b/packages/multimedia/ffmpeg/patches/rpi/0002-v4l2_req-hevc-leave-the-decode-queue-on-dst-failure.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..478788b839
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/multimedia/ffmpeg/patches/rpi/0002-v4l2_req-hevc-leave-the-decode-queue-on-dst-failure.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_req: hevc: leave the decode queue when no dst buffer is free
+
+v4l2_request_hevc_start_frame() adds the frame to the decode queue before
+it allocates its destination buffer. When that allocation fails, the
+frame stays queued and is never removed, so a later decode waits on it
+forever, and closing the decoder (avcodec_free_context) hangs. Remove it
+from the queue on that error path.
+
+Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_req_hevc_vx.c	2026-11-07 11:54:20
++++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_req_hevc_vx.c	2026-11-07 11:54:29
+@@ -767,6 +767,7 @@
+     {
+         if ((rd->qe_dst = mediabufs_dst_qent_alloc(ctx->mbufs, ctx->dbufs)) == NULL) {
+             av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "%s: Failed to get dst buffer\n", __func__);
++            decode_q_remove(&ctx->decode_q, &rd->decode_ent);
+             return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
+         }
+     }
-- 
